//Library compilation (no main): a lambda default on an exportable
//declaration is rejected at the producer — the cross-module wire carries
//no closure, so importing modules could never evaluate it. Capturing a
//formal parameter is fine inside the producing module; it is the export
//that the scope sentence names.
int step(int n, func<int,int> g = (x) -> x + n) { return g(n); }
